//? Title: Wishart and inverse-Wishart covariance matrices
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en

> Draw positive-definite matrices on a specified scale

The scale matrix has diagonal entries 2 and 1 and an off-diagonal
entry of 0.4. With 9.5 degrees of freedom in dimension 2, the Wishart
mean is 9.5 times the scale. The inverse-Wishart mean is the scale
divided by 6.5. Both laws allow fractional degrees of freedom.

The program compares the simulated diagonal means to those values.
It also evaluates the two log densities at the same positive-definite
matrix.

```{cpp, id=wishart-covariance-draws, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/random/matrix_distributions.hpp>
#include <print>

int main() {
    using namespace datamunge::random;
    using Matrix = datamunge::linalg::DenseMatrix<double>;
    const Matrix scale(2, 2, {2, .4, .4, 1}), point(2, 2, {5, 1, 1, 3});
    constexpr double df = 9.5;
    constexpr int repetitions = 10000;
    SplitMix64 rng(42);
    double ordinary = 0, inverse = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < repetitions; ++i) {
        ordinary += wishart_sample(rng, df, scale)(0, 0);
        inverse += inverse_wishart_sample(rng, df, scale)(0, 0);
    }
    std::println("| Law | Expected first diagonal | Simulated first diagonal | Log density at point |");
    std::println("| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |");
    std::println("| Wishart | {:.3f} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} |",
                 df * scale(0, 0), ordinary / repetitions, wishart_log_pdf(point, df, scale));
    std::println("| Inverse-Wishart | {:.3f} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} |",
                 scale(0, 0) / (df - 3), inverse / repetitions, inverse_wishart_log_pdf(point, df, scale));
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Law | Expected first diagonal | Simulated first diagonal | Log density at point |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Wishart | 19.000 | 18.867 | -9.171 |
| Inverse-Wishart | 0.308 | 0.309 | -26.042 |
// result_end

